WEBVTT

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.910
anata ni tazuneraretara watashi

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.910
あなたに尋ねられたら私

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.910
When you come visit me

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.650
nikkori hohoemu deshou

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.650
にっこり微笑むでしょう

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.650
I'll probably break into a big smile

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.630
umaku ienai kedo subete ga

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.630
うまく言えないけどすべてが

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.630
I can't really put it into words

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.710
totemo totemo kageyaitemasu

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.710
とてもとても輝いてます

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.710
but everything is shining oh so bright

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:47.600
kitto ima goro minna atsumattemasu

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:47.600
きっと今頃皆集まってます

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:47.600
I bet everyone is together right about now

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:53.330
sore wa sawagashikute

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:53.330
それは騒がしくて

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:53.330
It may get a little rowdy

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:58.810
demo itoshii

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:58.810
でもいとしい

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:58.810
but I wouldn't have it any other way

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:04.810
tonde ikimasu itsumo no tokoro e

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:04.810
飛んでいきますいつもの所へ

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:04.810
Let's fly away to our usual place

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:10.790
taiyou takaku ashita mo hare desu

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:10.790
太陽高く明日も晴れです

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:10.790
Tomorrow will be clear with the sun in the sky

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.590
moshi mo sukoshi sabishiku nattemo

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.590
もしも少し寂しくなっても

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.590
Even if you get a little lonely

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.100
daijoubu chanto miteimasu

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.100
大丈夫ちゃんと見ています

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.100
it's okay, I'll be watching

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.600
koko de

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.600
ここで

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.600
right here

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.030
It's gotten cold out...

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.990
Now for another day of hard work!

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:55.910
Good morning, Minawa. It's about time to get up.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.490
G-Good mor...

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.850
I'm sorry.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.260
You and that low blood pressure of yours...

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:10.530
Minawa, it's morning. You're starting school today.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:11.990
School...

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.440
I'm supposed to wake up before you and help out. I'm sorry.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:23.080
You don't have to apologize. Now, go wash your face.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:23.950
Sure.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:25.620
Um...

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:26.430
Yes?

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.390
Good morning...

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.270
Big sister.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.790
<b>Shiver!</b>

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:38.160
Minawa, who appeared one day in front of Suguru and me,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:42.330
...is assisting me around the house as an apprentice maid.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.810
Also, since she is 14 like Suguru,

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.860
...she is going to attend school starting today.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:56.440
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:56.440
<b>From Today On, You Are Minawa</b>

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.950
G-Good morning.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.590
M-Morning.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:11.570
Oh, you're going to school, so your school uniform would have been fine.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:13.700
Please, let me help out with something.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:17.410
Okay, divide the salad into those bowls, then.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.110
Okay.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:19.770
Morning!

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:25.060
Oh, good morning, Suguru. Minawa, say hello to him, too.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.380
I already did.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:27.840
I see.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:31.670
Breakfast will be ready soon, so please have a seat while you're waiting.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.400
Okay.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:36.480
All right, pour Suguru his coffee first.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:37.350
Okay.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.120
T-Thank you...

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.520
B-Big sister! Big sister!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.420
Suguru, are you all right?!

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.120
I'm sorry.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.890
Before you leave the house, you say "See you later."

00:03:58.490 --> 00:03:59.830
Oh, right. See you later.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.390
Let's get going! We'll be late!

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.730
Take care, you two.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.360
Mahoro, aren't you worried?

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.850
Of course I'm worried.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.580
I'm worried about whether or not she'll get used to school.

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:16.020
That's not what I mean!

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:21.290
She's a Management cyborg, right? Sure, she says she's a deserter, but...

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.230
That's Minawa you're talking about! You don't need to worry about that.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.340
H-Hey...

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.920
I won't forgive anyone who harms her, no matter who they are!

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.110
B-But it's you I'm worried about...

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.790
That's all I have to say!

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.850
But the thing is, one false step on their part...

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:42.550
...and they'll have a far worse crowd than Saint to deal with, Mahoro.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:49.180
Nobody knows when they came into being in this world.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.340
Perhaps they already existed at the time man first learned...

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.970
...to survive by depending on each other.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:07.260
They are the unseen shadow rulers who have manipulated history, nations, humanity itself...

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:11.540
...from behind a curtain of shadows, ever stepping out onto the stage.

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.470
They do not like events that aren't in the script.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.110
They do not allow uninvited visitors.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.420
This is because they are "The Management"

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:26.670
...they who move this world from the past to the present, and on into the future.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.490
I'm told that construction on the flagship is behind schedule.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.460
Yes, sir. You needn't worry.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.840
The technical problem was resolved by altering the construction method.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.260
There will be no change in her completion date.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.790
Any change in Saint's activity?

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.150
Their military activity has remained stopped since summer.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.460
On the other hand, the number of small craft flown for publicity is increasing.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.510
What of Vesper?

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.680
The same as Saint. We've seen no overt activity from them in some time.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:03.100
Vesper is one thing, but why would Saint maintain their silence?

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.720
Doctor Canan, let's hear your opinion on this matter.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:07.910
Yes, sir.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.780
Saint is a life form that has long forgotten war.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:18.540
This being the case, perhaps their combat technology itself is beginning to peak.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:20.760
You're suggesting they are standing by idly?

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.720
Indeed.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.360
The fact of the matter is that the weapons we have developed in the past year...

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:30.250
...are far superior to those of the aliens, efficiency-wise.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.390
Your junkyard battlebots can't even capture a single reject cyborg,

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.540
and do nothing but gobble up funds.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.890
I hear they were all set on their ears.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.510
Hey! How do you know that?!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.920
I mean, I was just about to get to that in my report, but...

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.620
Mephlis! In the first place, they were your--

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:52.950
I'm so sorry.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:07:00.350
However, to sum up, my reject was smarter than your alarm system, right?

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.520
I am truly sorry.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.610
Although I'm the one who was smarter.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:12.020
No, it was V-1046R MAHORO that destroyed the Man-Eaters, not your cyborg!

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.700
If she hadn't shown up...

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.480
Due to the loss of three prototype Man-Eaters,

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:19.910
...a serious delay is predicted in the mass production schedule.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.700
The resulting damages to Management,

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:26.140
...including repercussions, are approximately 59 million dollars.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.390
The rules stipulate that Dr. Canan will assume joint liability of 10% of said damages.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:34.900
A loan has been prepared, so please make use of it.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:40.970
The operation to capture escaped cyborg, code 370, was a failure.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:47.660
At present, 370 is in the protective custody of Vesper android V-1046R MAHORO.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.630
Does this mean it's fallen into Vesper's hands?!

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:52.900
Vesper's artificial human...

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:58.590
I heard that she's retired, but she's not someone to be trifled with.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:07:59.460
Yes, sir.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:05.320
First of all, Dr. Mephlis' cyborgs are nothing more than, if I may say, imitation androids.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:10.550
Even though it has been captured by Vesper, it is nothing to be alarmed about.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.800
Professor, you must remain calm.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.480
I know that! Damn, you're irritating.

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:16.180
I was made to be that way.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.300
Even if we resume the capture and recovery operation,

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:22.770
we'll only waste our resources and rouse a sleeping dragon.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.990
It will not be to our advantage in any way.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.840
You stare down at your feet and you say you've won?

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.970
Let me give you one piece of advice.

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:36.500
Be well warned that groundless optimistic conjectures are the cause of ruin.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.040
We are the ones who are standing by idly!

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:45.760
And now, I hear that Saint and Vesper are even expected to join forces in the future.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:49.500
If that happens, we would be unable to stop them!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.870
Watch your tongue, Mephlis!

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.620
Know your place, you measly repair man.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.310
You should've kept to one piece of advice.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:58.930
Well, never mind.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.420
In any event, we have no choice but to fight.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.520
If we cave in and accept the alien invasion,

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:13.880
...political, economic, military, every balance of power around the world will collapse,

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:18.260
...and the people of Earth will likely become a different race, one that is not human.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:22.600
That is nothing less than an impediment to our healthy evolution.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:26.020
Anything that threatens rule of the people of Earth...

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:30.090
...must be eliminated using our full power as Management.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:33.840
Gentlemen, the day of the final confrontation is almost upon us!

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:37.810
We shall fight together for the future of the Earth!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:46.660
Vesper wants friendship between the people of Earth and aliens.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:50.710
We may finally be forced to crush them both this time.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:53.570
What brought that on?

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:55.580
I don't have a cold, but these past few minutes, I've--

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.770
Slash? Slash!

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.170
I wanted to ask him to get something from the store.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.490
I wonder where he went?

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:04.440
He wouldn't!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.010
No, that could never happen. I made him stop, after all.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.480
By the way, I wonder if Minawa is doing okay at school?

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:21.590
It should be all right because Suguru and his friends are with her, but...

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:29.290
I'm too worried!

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:44.860
Hey, Minawa!

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.420
We've got art class next! C'mon, let's get to the other classroom.

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:50.490
Oh, right.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.210
Minawa!

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.210
Minawa!

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.970
Geez, not again...

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:04.720
Hey, are you okay?

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.910
I-I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:13.480
Hey, your forehead is bleeding.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.870
Let's go to the nurse's office!

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:18.740
For Mahoro's little sister, she sure is a klutz.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:19.580
Yeah.

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:23.950
Management's artificial human...

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.460
What is her objective in infiltrating the Misato household?

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.210
Oh, it's just you, Slashie.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.410
Don't get fresh with me, jerk!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.160
You're no fun.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.220
So, what's her story?

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.330
Whatever it is, she hasn't slipped up yet.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:47.400
However, I'm not a softhearted sap like those fools Mahoro and Suguru.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:52.130
If she makes me the least bit suspicious, I'll kill her.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.680
In that case, we feel the same way.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.910
Let's get one thing straight. You and me are enemies.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.810
It's not like I trust you.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:03.320
If you have a problem with me, just bare your fangs at me again.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:05.900
You're no fun.

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:17.310
I can't believe I did that. I flew too far and went all the way to Taipei.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.620
I'm finally down to a boxed lunch with rice and a single pickled plum...

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:26.220
This won't even keep me going until dinner.

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:30.120
If I'm in a sudden Ultra Fight with Mr. Misato after school in the gym equipment shed,

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.250
I'll never win!

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:32.670
M-Ms. Shikijo!

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:33.670
Oh, my!

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:38.850
So, you're planning on coming to the house again for another free meal, hm?

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:40.750
Maybe I'll hit her with a rock.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:46.210
That boiled white radish I ate for dinner last night sure was good...

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:51.810
Honestly, she's such a handful!

00:12:57.010 --> 00:13:02.040
Chinese dumplings from Heaven! This has to be a handout from God!

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.120
More like a handout from a maid.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:09.720
Oh, there she is! Mina--

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:18.840
Mr. Ryuga and Slash?

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:23.800
Ma...horo?

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:25.700
<b>TRIP</b>

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:25.740
<b>TRIP</b>

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:25.780
<b>TRIP</b>

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:25.950
<b>TRIP</b>

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.030
Oh, my god!

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:32.740
Geez, that was close!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.530
Wow, you scared me!

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:36.820
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:41.570
U-Uh, no... Are you always apologizing, Minawa?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.020
It's because I was always scolded.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:49.180
Uh, you don't have to, uh, apologize to me, okay?

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:55.880
Hey, what's up, Suguru?

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:57.620
Oh, not much...

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.140
Oh, no! It's a ground ball!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:09.790
Run!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.030
<b>TRIP</b>

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:13.160
Safe!

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.760
Yeah, Minawa! Talk about determination!

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:19.240
Although it sorta looked like she tripped on herself.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.030
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:22.240
Er, no, uh...

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:23.940
Still...

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:28.960
Look at all the boys!

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:33.980
What are they doing here all together like this?

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:37.810
Suguru, don't stop moving! Your side's open!

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:38.790
Oh, no!

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:40.700
Let's go, Suguru!

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:42.790
Clear!

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.870
Hamaji, you idiot!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.740
Minawa, look out!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.650
What are they doing?

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:10.440
Are you okay?

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:29.370
Oh, my god! Ms. Shikijo got flattened by a street light!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.080
Minawa, hold on!

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.540
You don't have to laugh so hard about it!

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:47.470
Mahoro, you must be an idiot.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:53.020
For instance, I bet you're dumb enough to eat a snail, thinking it was escargot.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.440
As if I'd make a mistake like that!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:16:00.180
You know, there was one time when this twit ate some weird mushrooms in the mountains...

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:03.020
...and spent all night rolling with laughter!

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:02.020
Don't eat mushrooms off the ground.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.550
But they're pretty good!

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:05.530
What, really?!

