satellite poem

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:10.760
<b>The empty classroom at dusk.</b>

00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:15.080
<b>Sparkling light floods in and gently wraps me in its warmth.</b>

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:19.920
<b>The wind blows in firmly and carries me into the sky.</b>

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:22.460
<b>Here, there is peace. Here, there is warmth.</b>

00:23:22.730 --> 00:23:27.320
<b>Here are the supple bonds I formed with my students.</b>

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:30.330
<b>The empty classroom at dusk.</b>

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:34.240
<b>When tomorrow comes, I wonder if I will form new bonds?</b>

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:38.860
<b>Ah, once again I will be able to feel my purpose in life as a teacher, won't I?</b>

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:43.810
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:47.490
Depending on who you ask, there seem lots of people...

00:23:47.490 --> 00:23:49.700
who fret about things in life both big and small.

00:23:50.210 --> 00:23:55.600
However, that sort of thing goes in and out of fashion depending on the era.

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:58.960
One person may love strawberries, while another loves watermelons.

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:02.380
Likes and dislikes depend on individual taste, so why not just leave it at that?

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:05.450
So, Mahoro, don't let it bother you so much, okay?

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:10.800
<b>Episode 3</b>

